ure"},{"text":"State management"},{"text":"API integration"},{"text":"Form handling"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Routing"},{"text":"Error handling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"React Ecosystem"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"React Router"},{"text":"TanStack Query"},{"text":"Redux Toolkit or equivalent state management"},{"text":"Next.js"},{"text":"Component libraries"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CSS"},{"type":"p","text":"Become strong in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Flexbox"},{"text":"CSS Grid"},{"text":"Animations"},{"text":"Transitions"},{"text":"CSS variables"},{"text":"Responsive layouts"},{"text":"Container queries"},{"text":"Modern CSS architecture"}]}]},{"heading":"Design-to-Code Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A UI/UX Engineer should be able to take:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Figma","Design System","Components","Code","Testing","Production"]},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Figma Design","Design Tokens","React Components","Storybook","API Integration","Responsive Testing","Accessibility Testing","Production Deployment"]},{"type":"p","text":"This ability is one of the strongest differentiators for the role."}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Product Engineering & Advanced UX","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on production-quality applications."},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced UX"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX metrics"},{"text":"A/B testing"},{"text":"Conversion optimization"},{"text":"Behavioral analytics"},{"text":"Usability evaluation"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Design systems"},{"text":"Information architecture"},{"text":"Product discovery"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Frontend"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Performance optimization"},{"text":"Server-side rendering"},{"text":"Static generation"},{"text":"Web accessibility"},{"text":"Progressive Web Apps"},{"text":"Browser performance"},{"text":"Security fundamentals"},{"text":"Testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unit testing"},{"text":"Component testing"},{"text":"End-to-end testing"},{"text":"Visual regression testing"},{"text":"Cross-browser testing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Jest/Vitest"},{"text":"React Testing Library"},{"text":"Playwright"},{"text":"Cypress"},{"text":"Storybook"}]}]},{"heading":"Accessibility Engineering","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Accessibility should be treated as an engineering requirement rather than an optional design feature."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"WCAG concepts"},{"text":"Semantic HTML"},{"text":"Keyboard navigation"},{"text":"Focus management"},{"text":"Screen readers"},{"text":"Accessible forms"},{"text":"Color contrast"},{"text":"ARIA"},{"text":"Accessible interactive components"},{"text":"A UI/UX Engineer should be able to identify and fix accessibility problems in both designs and code."}]}]},{"heading":"UX Research & Product Analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to make design decisions using evidence."},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Competitive analysis"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"User journey analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conversion rate"},{"text":"Retention"},{"text":"Engagement"},{"text":"Drop-off"},{"text":"Funnel analysis"},{"text":"Task completion rate"},{"text":"Time on task"},{"text":"Feature adoption"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Google Analytics"},{"text":"Microsoft Clarity"},{"text":"Hotjar or similar platforms"},{"text":"Mixpanel"},{"text":"Amplitude"}]}]},{"heading":"AI for UI/UX Engineering","kind":"other","blocks":[{"